#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096445 :question/id #uuid "069b2882-f4a9-589f-a903-4e89d077cd85" :question/math-academy-id "e-4279" :question/problem "Suppose, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$ and $\\mathbf{b} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$. Given that $7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\lambda \\left(3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b} \\right)$ are equal vectors, find the scalar factor $\\lambda$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\n7\\mathbf{a}+14\\mathbf{b}= \\dfrac{7}{3} (3\\mathbf{a}+6\\mathbf{b})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096446 :question/id #uuid "d1329498-4413-5d87-a814-be0d57a3afd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4280" :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf a$ is shown in the diagram below. Draw the vectors $2\\mathbf a$ and $-3\\mathbf a$.\n\n![](images/a5/a5eaa8baaf303ecbfa6c0fb207d6b19836cc90fc331e238cd473109f44fddf80.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $2\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ must be parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2\\mathbf{a}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $2\\mathbf{a}$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\n![](images/41/41eba7e6c5bbe420418726bd45efa668dc6be5ff5144ba35d52b53a43925c333.png)\n\nNext, for the vector $-3\\mathbf{a}$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $3\\mathbf{a}$ is $3$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $-3\\mathbf{a}$ have opposite directions since the factor $-3$ is negative.\n\n![](images/ed/eda3f2572d98ef1789292ec6d35569487b32efa459673dcb95f8fdd0d1f4ae5b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096494 :question/id #uuid "11c09a26-0e83-5a77-b777-aea8a3594960" :question/math-academy-id "e-5183" :question/problem "Consider the diagram that is shown below. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $\\mathbf{b}=-\\mathbf{c}$\n2. $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$\n3. $\\mathbf{a}=2\\mathbf{e}$\n\n![](images/95/95ae711c1ccbf7543e6d269aa8d817a66e2ac348113ea71f3a1babcbb23d1ca3.png)" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ have different magnitudes. So, $\\mathbf{b} \\neq -\\mathbf{c}$.\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{e}$ are parallel and have the same direction. Also, the magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{e}=2\\mathbf{a}$.\n- Statement III is false. The magnitude of $\\mathbf{e}$ is greater than the magnitude of $\\mathbf{a}$. So, $\\mathbf{a} \\neq 2\\mathbf{e}$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84bcbe16-7536-5125-b103-ef9c458c9db5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6c501b98e6eb5b998b6ebf822ec33e23dc1e67c01e3424e571ac19ded016a9a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093783} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d252a8-1a3a-531e-aba7-030ccb0e8aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fafda2acdd5a0f4355abcb067afff9367a5cf10acbe0b22f976e165927c18968.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093784} {:answer/id #uuid "35f79dfb-e1f1-5ee4-86af-f6afc25792cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a1/a173c48fb3f47049dbf06ccaf4628313b367bdc0b7b2c18bd7a88a7ed33a2069.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093785} {:answer/id #uuid "38cf6707-6d85-5651-82d6-d2a22b325ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b48a668105d698a5c055839f09d7a10c9b5b8da63bc05ca5a948bb6eb3df730.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093786} {:answer/id #uuid "748ec053-3c16-52b1-aa52-badc0e6e736e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d230aec47e23f7e1c8b03eeb2487b2c59d83e33bb1901b55070dd5