f the following diagrams shows the vectors $2a$ and $-\\frac{3}{2}a$?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $2a$ and $-\\frac{3}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $2a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2a$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $2a$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\nNext, for the vector $-\\frac{3}{2}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{3}{2}a$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{3}{2}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{3}{2}$ is negative.\n\nThe required vectors are shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7f63c606fff90d3d867a8b24a50855cc66c0fbb9e97748f429f5a53641f29c67.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23a46beb-967a-5086-b5eb-9b2fb499ded6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bcbc4dbb8e224b898bc8f521a739614e88348d75fbea1f372f039d4c7d3682a5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503935} {:answer/id #uuid "61a57ce0-507f-5d97-9844-b37c1b065395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21416fe41ffb466f862b849e0a6b63b3b8796074dff48311d9fb136431af34e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503955} {:answer/id #uuid "6785c6b0-c60f-5a4a-a2fb-dfb934c635b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bc/bca3d69121cab009870468c0e06a632e1c862a5d772d2f3b11fbd5e0409723dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503959} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9f8ff6-2066-574c-b8bc-a0f3e02b1196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/307c5223948f68dfeecabf81d5b0c4e0f8c2bd6588bb55b7c5b1baffaac2e96b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503980} {:answer/id #uuid "a15134ca-c6a0-5a19-b696-090f0ce08e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/im