swer/id #uuid "0821bfbf-d3f3-5791-86f1-89c62a946047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504746} {:answer/id #uuid "450ca3ad-5fc3-517b-9eb1-c3435fb1a849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504783} {:answer/id #uuid "5b80624b-1796-588d-a524-36a238a9c3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504787} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd81ae2-7ef1-5cbd-bfba-d3bcbf8f27ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504822} {:answer/id #uuid "df3d40c2-8d37-512a-94bc-0ead51b2e947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b80624b-1796-588d-a524-36a238a9c3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504787} :answer-field/id #uuid "2687c3e4-7ba0-5797-a128-d4fd2dc3a424" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0803379b-a2dd-51ec-9c3c-dfbd721fe7b8" :question/problem "Given that $λ(5a - 25b)$ and $6a - 30b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(5a - 25b)=λ(5)a+λ(-25)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{6}{5} = \\frac{6}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-30}{-25} = \\frac{6}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n6a - 30b=\\frac{6}{5}(5a - 25b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ed79da2-cd03-5afb-9f7b-d83a004a3e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504779} {:answer/id #uuid "9119d6e8-112d-5ec4-b34f-64b7967c9cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504806} {:answer/id #uuid "95b4ce27-3bec-5cfb-b356-53f9f4f1cf23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504807} {:answer/id #uuid "d37204b9-b5ff-512b-b51f-9c30c1240fe4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504827} {:answer/id #uuid "e4140720-5a44-55db-ba52-36637d99f99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95b4ce27-3bec-5cfb-b356-53f9f4f1cf23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504807} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c3cfc3c-9090-5c9c-9996-c40a0de36ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0ecb5994-c9d9-519e-8505-fb41a7d19179" :question/problem "Given that $-8a - 10b$ and $λ(20a + 25b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(20a + 25b)=λ(20)a+λ(25)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-8}{20} = -\\frac{2}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-10}{25} = -\\frac{2}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-8a - 10b=-\\frac{2}{5}(20a + 25b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b9dcace-dd91-581c-866e-f6d1aa1b2cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504770} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb644e7-b21f-5fce-8ff0-497d610ecaa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504775} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf206f0-3208-5daf-92b4-982429991a3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504798} {:answer/id #uuid "8355501f-d15e-5901-913e-d30d08a04672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504800} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b2c6bf-5dbe-54b3-abdf-e2d66204b501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bb644e7-b21f-5fce-8ff0-497d610ecaa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504775} :answer-field/id #uuid "64e7c313-092b-5316-b111-b5874ef1f27d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14ea91d3-f94c-5dd9-b51c-cb8c953c07f2" :question/problem "Given that $-3a - 24b$ and $λ(0.5a + 4b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b)=λ\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)a+λ(4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-3}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-24}{4} = -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-3a - 24b=-6(\\frac{1}{2}a + 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504768 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d3f1c2f-be82-53cd-aff4-7e5521c7167f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504749} {:answer/id #uuid "2eca6419-7234-51d4-b873-e7f3bd1bacf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504772} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4d6bea-566b-5d1a-8261-205958a929e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504784} {:answer/id #uuid "6aeefdc9-79a6-53eb-956a-d3afdf335860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504794} {:answer/id #uuid "f889768d-c9e5-5cf4-906b-9103278e26a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b4d6bea-566b-5d1a-8261-205958a929e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504784} :answer-field/id #uuid "7de5c44f-68ff-569f-b35c-cf4b217b5b0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "281e43ed-d77f-5100-ba06-3efb56464379" :question/problem "Given that $λ(0.25a - 3b)$ and $-a + 12b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{4}a - 3b)=λ\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)a+λ(-3)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{4}} = -4 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{12}{-3} = -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a + 12b=-4(\\frac{1}{4}a - 3b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-4\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41e50957-4074-51ce-b3ce-a17bd4649d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504781} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbf4a4b-2962-57b0-8fa0-f9e9c906d3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504788} {:answer/id #uuid "8f15975b-3796-5103-bca7-e86cdd8b32d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504804} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e8ed52-49b8-5508-83f2-0a518221e17d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504814} {:answer/id #uuid "e6534378-b2e2-53ba-bb3b-f131517f27d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41e50957-4074-51ce-b3ce-a17bd4649d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504781} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5afbb7d-33d0-521b-8a95-85f1371b282e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504810}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "315d6a79-c820-530f-a728-86a6ee67757a" :question/problem "Given that $18a + 45b$ and $λ(4a + 10b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(4a + 10b)=λ(4)a+λ(10)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{18}{4} = \\frac{9}{2} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{45}{10} = \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n18a + 45b=\\frac{9}{2}(4a + 10b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=\\frac{9}{2}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e5e0638-98ae-509c-9732-628564357b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504758} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0b57e6-adad-5ab1-b50c-baa08f8436f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504759} {:answer/id #uuid "57ec9105-4d5a-545d-a1cc-a71a9c8d87ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504785} {:answer/id #uuid "b784a5ac-2080-54be-91d4-3c1c534d613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504817} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf54d7b-b43e-54a1-a798-50b6c290222d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e5e0638-98ae-509c-9732-628564357b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504758} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba1896a9-56b0-5883-99fb-7c31d7375589" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "40a6d99d-54df-5f7a-8a53-416c89a4a6f9" :question/problem "Given that $-16a - 12b$ and $λ(20a + 15b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(20a + 15b)=λ(20)a+λ(15)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-16}{20} = -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-12}{15} = -\\frac{4}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-16a - 12b=-\\frac{4}{5}(20a + 15b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-\\frac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a70bf55-c653-524c-80de-799ed5e85c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504748} {:answer/id #uuid "24002d8c-909b-5291-810c-e5b512ab3ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504763} {:answer/id #uuid "861a84cc-037d-5823-98fb-0e7916753da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504801} {:answer/id #uuid "be08b6ee-3f5b-5095-bf94-57faac71a3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504819} {:answer/id #uuid "d3462742-b08a-59ec-a6bb-6da7af0a2bac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24002d8c-909b-5291-810c-e5b512ab3ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504763} :answer-field/id #uuid "259cab0a-d5bb-5b13-95b4-7e9853cbe78f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "88ca6c0b-f159-58fc-adb2-cf4950ce3bfd" :question/problem "Given that $λ(3a + 4b)$ and $12a + 16b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a + 4b)=λ(3)a+λ(4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{12}{3} = 4 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{16}{4} = 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n12a + 16b=4(3a + 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=4\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2438aff0-ab25-5493-acd3-16779c6d559a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504764} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5ef801-76a2-5b16-8649-284183c85297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504778} {:answer/id #uuid "b10cffa3-7a64-5e77-8731-6a69b0a734f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504812} {:answer/id #uuid "dd13527d-060a-54b9-87d8-6313be05ca35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504828} {:answer/id #uuid "f99c1385-74f7-5705-afdf-249eede8f4bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b10cffa3-7a64-5e77-8731-6a69b0a734f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504812} :answer-field/id #uuid "44f8d74d-ea99-52f5-8a02-cff10be0fe8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8a8aa6aa-79a2-59ee-8afa-533036e8e56c" :question/problem "Given that $λ(3a - 4b)$ and $18a - 24b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a - 4b)=λ(3)a+λ(-4)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{18}{3} = 6 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-24}{-4} = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n18a - 24b=6(3a - 4b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=6\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "157ebf7b-87d9-5d09-aeb5-68c2d360d505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504756} {:answer/id #uuid "657a483d-6ec3-5f79-94a7-b33528b25a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504792} {:answer/id #uuid "7ca084b1-1ff1-5c1e-93e7-86baea3b3290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504797} {:answer/id #uuid "d0dbfd45-c1e7-5e0e-b182-bd0217a71902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504823} {:answer/id #uuid "f75d0b77-0554-5d4c-8d8f-338361e0988a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "657a483d-6ec3-5f79-94a7-b33528b25a40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504792} :answer-field/id #uuid "a62569f9-1eb8-5cf2-b8c2-b9c0f68eb327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c06fdca4-9c0f-5aba-ba3a-3f0cefff0623" :question/problem "Given that $24a - 8b$ and $λ(3a - b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(3a - b)=λ(3)a+λ(-1)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{24}{3} = 8 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-8}{-1} = 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n24a - 8b=8(3a - b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=8\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are the same because the factor is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d92bf8b-f09a-519e-b6c2-297a8dbbae50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504757} {:answer/id #uuid "6742f50f-0fc1-5cef-9bfc-a345a595db6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504793} {:answer/id #uuid "a142d2dd-1c1e-5f0b-b6cf-e6016f0ff340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504808} {:answer/id #uuid "b2bea5f0-8a2f-5d26-b298-26810baae035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504813} {:answer/id #uuid "fd39139a-489f-500a-bb43-0430f464ded4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $λ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2bea5f0-8a2f-5d26-b298-26810baae035" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504813} :answer-field/id #uuid "eac2129e-641b-514b-a9a0-d474e422aab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e813b171-b626-57db-af36-b0b2e170a174" :question/problem "Given that $λ(0.5a + 3b)$ and $-a - 6b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $λ$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that\n\n$$\nλ(\\frac{1}{2}a + 3b)=λ\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)a+λ(3)b.\n$$\n\nThe same scale factor must multiply the whole non-zero vector. Comparing the two coefficients gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nλ &= \\frac{-1}{\\frac{1}{2}} = -2 \\\\\nλ &= \\frac{-6}{3} = -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n-a - 6b=-2(\\frac{1}{2}a + 3b).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nλ=-2\n$$\n\nThe two non-zero vectors are parallel. Their directions are opposite because the factor is negative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186504834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11675813-ef33-5580-b5ab-30b652a490b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186504751} {:answer/id #uuid "15575bb1-