c-aad1-0f002a1758f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-69951" :question/problem "![](images/31/314cd1d2e150c078fa7232c81125de44fb8c26c176d2a1f32ab02fbae2eef299.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $m=-g$\n\nII. $a=z$\n\nIII. $g=-\\frac{1}{2}m$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The magnitude of $m$ is greater than the magnitude of $g.$ So, $m\\ne -g.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The vectors $a$ and $z$ have opposite directions. So, $a\\ne z.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, vectors $g$ and $m$ are parallel and have opposite directions. Also the magnitude of $g$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $m.$ So, $g=-\\frac{1}{2}m.$\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4834da0c-e138-5195-b5c7-e0793083032e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/2938ca5550faa3fb4c04daae1dc63a6dc86698a90a247fccd38fc034f5a7ff11.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571668} {:answer/id #uuid "70bf1955-e060-5bfb-849a-9bf126ad2269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae0235d72386ef97519d913dc5cef3da4699a92a18d5c037153020d75c21a3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571731} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2a1653-575b-52cd-a682-b2b19dca8b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1dc14e69e650dd9081cbfb3769e21d49aa905b6d8b3a84d9dfaf935ba57a107e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571815} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e27537-9585-5713-8d2f-71f44be2c767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b20f3879b4b9bd98aacd5bce58a1bc6241a2671e74ffb27374545acbe3975098.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571827} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4df393-61ca-5a1e-b8ec-00b075b26d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5df7bba8e49cecb0ce082a7e8093478c032c90eae1ebccd5b3b3efed825b6f63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea4df393-61ca-5a1e-b8ec-00b075b26d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5df7bba8e49cecb0ce082a7e8093478c032c90eae1ebccd5b3b3efed825b6f63.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571952} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c52a915-0f05-5bb2-9874-890dcfeb7473" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571989}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9199d3db-0aa2-51c3-b858-22576fdfaa53" :question/math-academy-id "q-69960" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b2c3f59df41cb406ddfc41eea81a979dec578ba990032f0ff4f2f9792f58c8b2.png)\n\nThe vector $a$ is depicted above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vectors $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ and $2a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ and $2a$ must be parallel to $a.$\n\nNow, for the vector $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ is $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{3}{4}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{3}{4}$ is negative.\n\n![](images/13/13e4de227344b9eb7d1867cca0d05d9bcb647662a0c732398b42277ac379d361.png)\n\n \n\nNext, for the vector $2a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $2a$ is twice the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $2a$ have the same direction since the factor $2$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](images/13/13ca18bebfdb3c738d0a1198d0ce4235bfd77185bcf232f79f9ba089ce3b6d38.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b8ce19e-7310-5653-bd81-7663f10f1275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/505d9eb880fb166f11d45858b34a2aa3491a6772da6266e1954c383ebc97a905.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571560} {:answer/id #uuid "10d35a2d-dc1a-5fbd-93b5-a142a14eec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fd554195222a46ab5fcefdb3ca601fdcba5a0daeba16ce3faae2bc6c9371bb3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571567} {:answer/id #uuid "34d29957-a4c2-51f3-8772-9c52f4ca375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c371c84dedc8f76fe286a7f4201416c2c344d4718bdf61a80bd5c3da7a048cd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571626} {:answer/id #uuid "878bf775-d689-5f90-935e-bdbb9216b91a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/ea348c364e2d05abb2adc5c86ce2d59e01ccc1c1d9e3e4ba7c189cc1cf3cb925.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571771} {:answer/id #uuid "8df859fc-145b-5e86-9c79-d402ed969101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/359aed8184fd2ae25a5290a013e68fb8068176286e8684cd13459df4e77e9693.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34d29957-a4c2-51f3-8772-9c52f4ca375c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c371c84dedc8f76fe286a7f4201416c2c344d4718bdf61a80bd5c3da7a048cd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571626} :answer-field/id #uuid "5428c292-72be-5b0f-bf8c-5686e732abae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "99744ab1-80a8-57ad-804e-15c6f48c9bd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-119064" :question/problem "![](images/60/605c5def8bc643f0f601f89b9f8d7b556ac94206867dbe8904ef746c83f02fc0.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vector $a.$ Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $\\frac{3}{2}a?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $\\frac{3}{2}a$ must be parallel to $a.$\nNow, we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $\\frac{3}{2}a$ is $\\frac{3}{2}$ of the magnitude of $a.$\n\n- Vectors $a$ and $\\frac{3}{2}a$ have the same direction since the factor $\\frac{3}{2}$ is positive.\n\nTherefore, the correct diagram is the following.\n\n![](images/59/591682cfbe0f50347d88f894f4c2b740fca140e8a93838f5c53022f9f50ee6da.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3406a2e-3e30-5a10-afce-d9b951b31dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3406a2e-3e30-5a10-afce-d9b951b31dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571887} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d6a9ee6-1f19-56a5-9ce3-6b062583c4af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9cb3a4aa-4089-5a0f-987c-888c6fdaeaf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-324233" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b)$ and $4\\sqrt{7}\\,a+7b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n4\\sqrt{7}\\,a+7b=\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{7}(4a+\\sqrt{7}b)=\\lambda (4a+\\sqrt{7}b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(4a+\\sqrt{7}b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=4a+\\sqrt{7}b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{7}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =\\sqrt{7}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b9401b-8227-5b31-a1af-489974f90cd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571693} {:answer/id #uuid "78af9df5-9c07-5149-afa4-47ce7f15a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571747} {:answer/id #uuid "89eb437f-1651-5f56-bd87-3dcb712156b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571775} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d91dc1-da76-5e69-bffc-16bb4177a79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571823} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f5c7ac-9844-58a6-b692-649d36bbf0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f5c7ac-9844-58a6-b692-649d36bbf0d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571947} :answer-field/id #uuid "14754df4-59b3-5598-a9e7-143bba8252f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a4c754c3-d143-5941-8c38-1a8c75e6be25" :question/math-academy-id "q-20395" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (12a-52b)$ and $-3a+13b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-3a+13b=\\lambda (12a-52b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{4}(12a-52b)=\\lambda (12a-52b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(12a-52b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=12a-52b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{4}u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b86a3d8-bbdc-510c-bdb1-25822dde58a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571647} {:answer/id #uuid "b55d5c71-dfbf-5d5c-b477-04b04d7dda95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571856} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ff3248-4b13-5d5b-9c41-dfbe5793add0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571900} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} {:answer/id #uuid "d66f4a36-7bf8-5c75-8d2c-1dec7887829a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4944-bf33-5ba6-9d6a-697b65a617dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186571909} :answer-field/id #uuid "471634b7-feb0-50b9-9eda-91e81c3b2ea0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f081ecc9-be21-500f-81d8-5fe5809e98ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-76939" :question/problem "![](images/92/9236e136f26433023d806181fcfbef9c05d4976f75e14f74840ae7f48a35da99.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $r=3q$\n\nII. $s=2t$\n\nIII. $p=-s$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $q$ have the opposite directions. So, $r\\ne 3q.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same directions. Also, the magnitude of $s$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t.$ So, $s=2t.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the opposite directions. Also, their magnitudes are the same. So, $p=-s.$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, and statement I is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186619791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e1a0ab1-a42d-5f77-bbde-5497f8faa861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619288} {:answer/id #uuid "7690831b-061f-52b4-aea8-c355a162ccae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619354} {:answer/id #uuid "cb681852-e397-5d26-896c-00a5f6714da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619504} {:answer/id #uuid "cd24efa4-64f4-5e2c-bf8d-9c527309ea32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619507} {:answer/id #uuid "cdec3b29-98b9-5b9a-9b62-3cdf35ced657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdec3b29-98b9-5b9a-9b62-3cdf35ced657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619508} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0de304-7026-5fa0-aae1-0f3de8c53dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b26b5414-ab10-5d8a-9dff-43df60b1ebb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20398" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b)$ and $4a+49b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n4a+49b=\\lambda (\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n14(\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b)=\\lambda (\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2}{7}a+\\frac{7}{2}b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n14u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\lambda =14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03c15dce-8511-5979-9b74-7ebbf9e5b88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626869} {:answer/id #uuid "5df61ea7-1388-5527-85c5-09542bc0397a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626879} {:answer/id #uuid "71f18c07-373c-5838-86f5-c9d3e7c0fad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626884} {:answer/id #uuid "afc97049-5218-5c78-8c23-e5961b668ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626893} {:answer/id #uuid "e46bad05-2257-5e82-a5ec-08e42861d2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03c15dce-8511-5979-9b74-7ebbf9e5b88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626869} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1bab941-decd-579d-9449-8ee4fbb31eda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a2750ba-f197-5682-92b7-49915f2e579e" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (-9a - 3b)$ and $-3a - b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-3a - b=\\lambda (-9a - 3b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}(-9a - 3b)=\\lambda (-9a - 3b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(-9a - 3b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=-9a - 3b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626886 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491869cb-e8f8-5a56-840c-33c1dd2172c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626876} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec3f5a6-87e4-5057-a436-a63062d94bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626878} {:answer/id #uuid "5e967b8b-3b6d-5148-b04f-dacb48a87afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626880} {:answer/id #uuid "aa786594-188d-527e-ade1-b3337e626e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626891} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b66e32-4aa5-5062-a9e8-a201947f1c6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ec3f5a6-87e4-5057-a436-a63062d94bb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626878} :answer-field/id #uuid "60f705bb-b24e-579b-a0b1-74f8f189a7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7ddcb09f-d936-51c0-b32f-d3fc378e3945" :question/problem "Given that $-3a - 3b$ and $\\lambda (-4a - 4b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-3a - 3b=\\lambda (-4a - 4b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}(-4a - 4b)=\\lambda (-4a - 4b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(-4a - 4b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=-4a - 4b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08bbfd24-8124-57a6-b62b-c9a511ff3665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626870} {:answer/id #uuid "1aea1971-8622-5b0a-801c-02ad5a976873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626873} {:answer/id #uuid "6aeed310-d799-536f-b938-9f4d764cb49e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626883} {:answer/id #uuid "ac903ca7-478c-50f8-aa73-e250866d7dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626892} {:answer/id #uuid "c21015ae-7c06-5f96-b853-f07e7b8418da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c21015ae-7c06-5f96-b853-f07e7b8418da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626896} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a39943f-ef83-51b5-abde-0be167954982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626882}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "91f11ac1-0ccf-569d-8135-b0deec65e469" :question/problem "Given that $\\lambda (4a + 7b)$ and $-8a - 14b$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n-8a - 14b=\\lambda (4a + 7b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n-2(4a + 7b)=\\lambda (4a + 7b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(4a + 7b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=4a + 7b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n-2\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194ecd34-c228-5a04-89a0-367d0686de06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626872} {:answer/id #uuid "31edfeae-7d1d-5972-a7a9-5fe425db14a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626874} {:answer/id #uuid "98d9dc0b-2a69-546d-8fe4-34e7a3fe84ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626890} {:answer/id #uuid "daef58f5-40ca-5779-b798-894c1317a8de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626899} {:answer/id #uuid "dd677fbb-f151-5f31-8636-dd617959684c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31edfeae-7d1d-5972-a7a9-5fe425db14a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626874} :answer-field/id #uuid "9207dfc6-4ff6-5785-9c78-f956731d22a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d7d88d93-65fb-5288-a8e2-b9c80080052e" :question/problem "Given that $16a + 20b$ and $\\lambda (4a + 5b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n16a + 20b=\\lambda (4a + 5b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n4(4a + 5b)=\\lambda (4a + 5b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(4a + 5b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=4a + 5b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n4\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186626898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b056ec5-4215-57db-a9cf-c5ad78c4efc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626875} {:answer/id #uuid "4be2a90b-4d98-5e7d-b80d-7e75b59153fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626877} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd4934b-8b93-5f03-a003-cd76030f7a1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No such $\\lambda$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626885} {:answer/id #uuid "b37eb20e-09eb-5b7d-b9fe-2201dfd903ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626894} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e05963-2f5d-5073-b8c9-2e42b2e03db6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b056ec5-4215-57db-a9cf-c5ad78c4efc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626875} :answer-field/id #uuid "920095dc-6720-58b1-9e3f-edd630232bcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186626888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9a96284-1ef3-5a64-9e94-11e42d4099f3" :question/problem "Given that $12a + 16b$ and $\\lambda (3a + 4b)$ are equal (non-zero) vectors, find the scale factor $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "Since the vectors are equal, we can write\n\n$$\n12a + 16b=\\lambda (3a + 4b).\n$$\n\nNext, we factor the left-hand side, which gives\n\n$$\n4(3a + 4b)=\\lambda (3a + 4b).\n$$\n\nNotice that we have $(3a + 4b)$ on both sides. So, let's define a new vector $u$ as\n\n$$\nu=3a + 4b.\n$$\n\nThen, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n4\\,u=\\lambda u.\n$$\n\nSince $u$ is non-zero,\n\n$$\n\\lambda=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069f92c7-15e9-50bb-83e7-0963ced055e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42068a3db6a1405e1aa5a0b45666ee7bbc03cdf0fb30895ef211f5e540f1cac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627940} {:answer/id #uuid "0c7671d4-f12e-59e2-81af-a05045b946ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c184c372b1dd3618f46ccb5a4ec7cb131cc6de29dc0641adc9cb54a516d7d3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627941} {:answer/id #uuid "4d488358-d1dc-5e0d-b147-24d6ee495e5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b1bc8c0f660d7e4098094e6885931bd2f2761f0df0c0c3aa1cf3a2d48816e13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627953} {:answer/id #uuid "65749755-a4df-5839-b8ae-efa3b7742370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6e/6e388db239b45de7820eac7e890a5bc6d925f7c0a02521a8ca6645ffbd638168.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627962} {:answer/id #uuid "d29ead10-2421-5098-9ad5-68cb2890b580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b2/b240905159ca4826364c659386dd767c25da47aa217aba317a1bc63f4a134737.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c7671d4-f12e-59e2-81af-a05045b946ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c184c372b1dd3618f46ccb5a4ec7cb131cc6de29dc0641adc9cb54a516d7d3d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627941} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4d680e-eb35-5584-a050-dc8a539f537a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0ff75e59-d487-59a2-85ed-84f065b11454" :question/problem "![](images/44/4435e904dc532907bc85ed8ac6ecd52b0320736e1ef2fa3e2746a40472577829.png)\n\nThe vector $a$ is depicted above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vectors $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ and $2a$?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that both $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ and $2a$ must be parallel to $a$.\n\nNow, for the vector $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ we have the following:\n\n- The magnitude of $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the magnitude of $a$.\n- Vectors $a$ and $-\\frac{1}{2}a$ have opposite directions since the factor $-\\frac{1}{2}$ is negative.\n\n![](images/4e/4e1721331e0fa7e4240b1d09426e57fdc8e48052bd72dd9733cbcc